 187: ## 6. SOC labels
 188: 
 189: Each mission begins fully charged under the published protocol. Telemetry SOC
 190: is coulomb-counted using the mission-specific interpolated capacity:
 191: 
 192: \[
 193: SOC_i=\operatorname{clip}_{[0,100]}\left(100+
 194: 100\frac{\sum_{k\le i} I_kdt_k/3600}{Q_m}\right).
 195: \]
 196: 
 197: For a phase, `dis_dSOC = SOC_end - SOC_start`. Capacity and SOH used for this
 198: calculation are target-construction data and are excluded from the predictor
 199: allow-list. Its mission aggregate, `dis_dSOC_sum`, is also labelled as target
 200: context and cannot enter the SOH or RUL predictor matrix. The separate
 201: `dis_dSOC_baseline` uses beginning-of-life capacity and remains an admissible
 202: physics-based predictor.
 203: 
 204: ## 7. Sliding-window samples
 205: 
 206: All windows use stride 1, left padding, a binary validity mask, and at least
 207: one observed time step. No window can cross a cell boundary; SOC windows also
 208: cannot cross a mission boundary.
 209: 
 210: | Task | Input ending at prediction time | Target | Maximum length |
 211: |---|---|---|---:|
 212: | SOC | Retained flight-phase features through phase `t` within one mission | Observed `dis_dSOC` at retained flight phase `t+1` | 16 phases |
 213: | SOH | Mission features through mission `m` | Non-negative SOH drop from `m` to `m+5` | 20 missions |
 214: | RUL | Mission features through mission `m` | Event-observed RUL at `m`, separately for 90%, 85%, and 80% | 20 missions |
 215: 
 216: For SOC, a group of length `n` creates at most `n-1` samples:
 217: 
 218: ```text
 219: for input_end in 0 .. n-2:
 220:     start &lt;- max(0, input_end - 16 + 1)
 221:     X &lt;- phase_features[start : input_end + 1]
 222:     y &lt;- dis_dSOC[input_end + 1]
 223: ```
 224: 
 225: For SOH and RUL, a mission at position `m` creates one sample when its target
 226: is finite and event-observed. The window is the latest 20 mission rows ending
 227: at `m`. Target columns are rejected if supplied in the predictor list.
 228: 
